{
  "title": "Swan Neck Deformity",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6013/swan-neck-deformity",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Dec 26 2022",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Swan Neck Deformities are degenerative conditions, often seen with rheumatoid arthritis, characterized by hyperextension of the PIP joint and flexion of the DIP joint due to an imbalance of muscle forces on the PIP.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with resting hyperextension of the PIP joint combined with resting flexion of the DIP joint of the involved digit.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is initially a course of PIP splinting to prevent hyperextension. In progressive cases, volar plate advancement with **central slip tenotomy** can be performed.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "EPIDEMIOLOGY",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "seen in up to 50% of patients with rheumatoid arthritis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pathophysiology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lax volar plate",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**imbalance of muscle forces on PIP** (extension force > flexion force)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Causes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Seen in **rheumatoid arthritis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Injuries include",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "MCP joint volar subluxation (rheumatoid arthritis)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "mallet finger",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "FDS laceration",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "intrinsic contracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PATHOanatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Primary lesion is **lax volar plate** that allows hyperextension of PIP. Causes include",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "trauma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "generalized ligament laxity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "rheumatoid arthritis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Secondary lesion is **imbalance of forces on the PIP joint** (PIP extension forces that is greater than the PIP flexion force). Causes of this include",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**mallet injury**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to transfer of DIP extension force into PIP extension forces",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**FDS rupture**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to unopposed PIP extension combined with loss of integrity of the volar plate",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**intrinsic contracture**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tethering of the lateral (collateral) bands by the transverse retinacular ligament as a result of PIP hyperextension.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "if the lateral (collateral) bands are tethered, excursion is restricted and the extension force is not transmitted to the terminal tendon, and is instead transmitted to the PIP joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**MCP joint volar subluxation**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "caused by rheumatoid arthritis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "snapping and locking of the fingers",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "hyperextension of PIP",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "flexion of DIP",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6013/images/swan_neck_deformity.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral view of the affected hand",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "double ring splint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "can prevent hyperextension of PIP",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "volar plate advancement and PIP balancing with **central slip tenotomy**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "progressive deformity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "address volar plate laxity with **volar plate advancement**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "correct PIP joint muscles imbalances with either",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**FDS tenodesis** indicated with FDS rupture",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**spiral oblique retinacular ligament reconstruction**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**central slip tenotomy (Fowler)**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
